# Weekly newsletter automation

When researching, writing, or sending the **Sunday weekly newsletter**:

1. Follow **`tools/weekly-newsletter/TWO_STAGE_WORKFLOW.md`** (Stage 1 research vs Stage 2 writing), then **`HOW_TO_ASSEMBLE.md`** and **`AGENT_RUNBOOK.md`**.
2. Topics: **final expense, whole life, term, IUL, annuities** only. Block Medicare/Medigap and unrelated P&C/health.
3. News period: prior Sunday–Saturday America/Chicago. Harvest ≥8 candidates when possible; evergreen only as background if thin; always **3** stories of **equal depth**.
4. Stage 1 must save and validate a research brief **before** Stage 2. Stage 2 writes from the brief only — no new news search. Do not use mini/economy models for Stage 2.
5. Follow **`tools/weekly-newsletter/CONTENT_PACKAGE.md`** (email stories ~175–250 words; one phone CTA in the close).
6. 6 a.m. Sunday Chicago send: **julie@ in Spanish**, **admin@ in English**.
7. Do not invent premiums. Do not publish the public blog until Julie asks (`newsletter-consumer-blog` rule). Keep the research brief for audit/blog.
8. Client letter only. Never: writing-method narration, “a news story does not cancel your policy,” “read every question slowly,” or “we do not have that file / we will not repeat a rate we did not verify.” Julie cut those because they sound weird. Omit unverified numbers silently.
9. After the approved blog and images are live, Facebook is automatic — `tools/weekly-newsletter/FACEBOOK_AUTOMATION.md`. Do not wait for a Tuesday/Thursday prompt.
